      <h2>S-Tier: The Gold Standard Treats</h2>

      <h3>1. Oreo® Cookie Blizzard Treat (The Undisputed King)</h3>
      <p>There is a reason the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo® Cookie Blizzard</a> remains Dairy Queen’s number-one seller across every franchise nationwide. The fine chocolate cookie dust subtly colors the vanilla soft serve, while coarser cookie chunks provide a crisp, satisfying crunch in every single spoonful. Because the sandwich cookie filling incorporates smoothly into cold dairy, you never get teeth-shattering frozen rocks. Starting at $3.49 for a Mini, it is the benchmark against which every other frozen treat is measured.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Flavor Profile:</strong> Deep cocoa wafers balanced by creamy vanilla soft serve</li>
        <li><strong>Texture Score:</strong> 10/10 — Perfect crumble ratio throughout the cup</li>
        <li><strong>Insider Pro Tip:</strong> Ask for an extra scoop of Oreo or swap vanilla soft serve for chocolate soft serve for a rich double-chocolate variation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough Blizzard Treat</h3>
      <p>For lovers of doughy chewiness, the <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough Blizzard</a> ranks right behind Oreo. DQ uses real, eggless chocolate chip cookie dough nuggets paired with decadent fudge drizzles. The dough maintains its pliable texture even when chilled below freezing, delivering a buttery, brown-sugar flavor explosion that pairs naturally with the silky DQ soft serve.</p>

      <h3>3. Royal New York Cheesecake Blizzard Treat</h3>
      <p>If you prefer complex desserts over pure candy sugar, the <a href="/items/royal-new-york-cheesecake-blizzard">Royal New York Cheesecake Blizzard</a> is perfection. Real graham cracker crust crumbles and rich cheesecake cubes are blended into soft serve, and the entire cup is anchored around a decadent core filled with real strawberry topping. Dipping your spoon into the center fruit reservoir cuts through the rich dairy creaminess effortlessly.</p>

      <h2>A-Tier: Heavy-Hitter Favorites</h2>

      <h3>4. Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's® Blizzard</a> is unapologetically rich. Chopped peanut butter cups create small specks of salty peanut paste alongside chocolate shell fragments. It is high in calories (starting around 360 cal for Mini and up to 1,000+ for Large), but for peanut butter diehards, nothing else compares.</p>

      <h3>5. Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster</a> is the premier "grown-up" Blizzard on the menu. Roasted, salted pecan halves are blended with silky caramel and chocolate cone dip. The contrast between warm buttery pecans, smooth caramel ribbons, and cold dairy creates one of the most sophisticated textures in fast food dessert history.</p>

      <h3>6. Choco Brownie Extreme Blizzard</h3>
      <p>Chocolate lovers, rejoice. The <a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard">Choco Brownie Extreme</a> brings chewy brownie chunks, rich cocoa fudge, and chocolate chunks all in one cup. It is intensely rich — so much so that even a Small size can easily satisfy two people.</p>

      <h2>How to Order Smarter: Pro Tips for Maximum Value</h2>
      <p>Getting the best possible Blizzard involves more than just picking a flavor. Keep these insider ordering tactics in mind on your next visit:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>The "Mini" Size is the Sweet Spot:</strong> With rich candy-packed flavors like Reese's or Brownie Extreme, the Mini ($3.49) provides the ideal portion size without tipping over into a sugar coma.</li>
        <li><strong>Ask for "Lightly Blended" for Chunkier Texture:</strong> If you love large candy bar chunks rather than fine crumbs, ask the crew member to pulse the spindle for a second less.</li>
        <li><strong>Remember the Upside-Down Guarantee:</strong> Dairy Queen guarantees that every Blizzard is served upside down or the next one is free at participating locations. If the server hands it to you right side up without flipping, politely inquire about the voucher!</li>
      </ol>

